    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0115" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/3260: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-04T04:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 4,
                                1919, 4 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:43
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>145. Under date of December 24, 5 p.m., Legation Stockholm informed the Mission
                    that the British, Italian, French Ministers and himself had received letters
                    dated Stockholm, December 23, from Litvinoff, a plenipotentiary of the Russian Federation of
                    Soviets, expressing a desire to enter upon preliminary peace negotiations.</p>
                <p>For your information. This matter is receiving consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
